+# Weight-only NVFP4 DFlash2
+
+Qwen3.8-27B DFlash2 components may store their projection, convolution and selector codebook matrices as weight-only NVFP4. Runtime binding preserves their codes, group scales, tensor divisors and tile-aligned subview offsets. Projection routes use BF16 activations; the selector accumulates conditional scores from represented FP32 codebook values and BF16 projected hidden states.
+
+Use a compatible `.ninfer` artifact containing the DFlash2 component and select `--spec dflash2 --draft-tokens 7`. See [DFlash semantics](../maintainer/dflash.md) for proposal distributions, target verification and context state. An optional selector confidence output reports the selected candidate's temperature-one probability.
+
+The selector tests cover independent FP64 references, direct and lattice schedules, batch and width boundaries, exact greedy selection, sampled proposal distributions, graph replay and confidence. Projection, convolution and context tests cover represented NVFP4 inputs at model geometries. These focused checks establish Op behavior; whole-model throughput, long-context quality and BF16-reference perplexity need their own measurements. The custom build is qualified on Linux consumer Blackwell; other platform results are not established here.
